DejaVu 2.1, pinned from commit
4c275e9ebac4fe51a26aac406682b9bcbfd03a9d (2026-08-13).

Upstream: https://github.com/markusa4/dejavu
License: MIT; see LICENSE.

Tactix compiles these headers only in
src/symmetry_backend/dejavu_backend.cpp, with exceptions and RTTI enabled, and
exposes a failure-safe noexcept boundary to the no-exception/no-RTTI core.

The source matches the pinned commit except for a narrow cooperative
termination hook in utility.h, dejavu.h, preprocess.h, dfs.h, bfs.h, and
rand.h. The hook only polls a caller callback and throws the private
termination_requested marker inside the exception-enabled backend. Tactix
catches that marker and translates it to Status::Interrupted before returning
through the noexcept boundary; it does not change graph or group results.

The additional groups.h extension accepts optional per-point orbit-size bounds
in random_schreier::set_base. Null retains the upstream path. Tactix supplies
the exact initial input-generator orbit sizes only for FixAndCutResift: every
later stabilizer is a subgroup, so these bounds remain valid. They permit the
existing completed-transversal fast path; they do not discard generators or
change which explicit SR tuples are legal. Generator-ID reuse experiments are
not included in this vendor patch.
